# The trigger has an intervening "if you've drawn more than one card this turn" and fires "on your turn": the card drawn as
# Proft's enters is one (turn 1), so nothing happens at beginning of combat; on turn 2 Bot1 draws three with Ancestral Recall in
# Bot2's upkeep, but it is not Bot1's turn, so the Ornithopter gets no counters then either.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Proft's Eidetic Memory
Ancestral Recall
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Proft's Eidetic Memory.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
